 "n_seeds": 20,
 "finding": "The mechanism replay would need is wired and it works, in the 1 of 20 seeds where it is switched on. MBON11 is GABAergic, carries more of the engram than any other cell, and the Kenyon cells it contacts are 1.86 times enriched for the trained ensemble, so depressing its input disinhibits that ensemble preferentially. Where it fires (untrained rate 0.537 Hz) the memory cuts its rate by 67% and the odour-A Kenyon cells speed up by +7.6%. Where it does not (untrained rate 0.001 Hz, 19 seeds) the ensemble moves by +0.02%, indistinguishable from nothing (p = 0.68). Every other engram-carrying MBON that does fire contacts the trained ensemble LESS than chance (MBON20 0.41x, MBON30 0.57x, MBON32 0.50x, MBON35 0.00x), so their disinhibition goes to the rest of the mushroom body and works against the trained ensemble standing out. What stands between this model and memory reactivation is therefore one number: how often MBON11 fires.",
